 PAH is a local Python project workspace that coordinates independently runnable tools without absorbing their internal logic.
 
+## PAH 0.6 — full tool workspaces
+
+PAH 0.6 keeps the 0.5 quick-context panels, but adds a persistent top-level work-mode switch:
+
+```text
+[ Workspace ] [ Analysis ] [ Documents ] [ References ]
+```
+
+- **Workspace** is the PAH-native file browser/editor/terminal/venv view.
+- **Analysis** hosts the existing full Code Repository Cataloguer interface against the current PAH workspace.
+- **Documents** hosts the existing full Research Document Workbench interface, scoped to the current PAH workspace.
+- **References** hosts the existing full Research Paper Repository Manager interface using the PAH-selected reference library.
+
+The three full interfaces are reused rather than reimplemented. PAH starts them lazily as internal loopback Flask servers on ports `8766`, `8767`, and `8768`, and displays them inside persistent PAH work-mode frames. This preserves their existing root-relative `/api/...` routes and standalone behavior without route collisions in the host server on port `8765`.
+
+The full tools remain optional: if a module is not installed, its quick panel and full-mode button report the missing module while PAH Workspace mode continues to work.
+
+### State handoff
+
+- Opening/switching a PAH workspace rebinds full **Analysis** to that repository.
+- Full **Documents** treats the current PAH workspace as its single document project and writes directly to the real project files. Heavy implementation directories such as `.git`, `.venv`, `venv`, `node_modules`, and caches are omitted from its document tree.
+- Selecting a reference library in PAH configures full **References** to the same library. A library changed inside the full reference manager is adopted back into the PAH quick-reference panel when returning.
+- Returning from a full tool refreshes clean PAH editor tabs from disk. Unsaved PAH tabs are never overwritten. Returning from full Analysis conservatively marks quick-panel analysis stale because the standalone refactor controls may have changed source files.
+
+### Contextual jumps
+
+The quick right panel now includes **Full**, **Full workspace**, and **Full manager** buttons so a selected task can expand into the specialized interface without giving up the lightweight overview surface.
+
 ## PAH 0.5
 
 PAH 0.5 is the first **cross-module workflow release**. The host still coordinates `CodeAnalyzer`, `DocumentEngine`, and `ReferenceManager` only through their public APIs, but it can now turn analysis/reference facts into traceable technical-documentation artifacts.
